r any limitations or restrictions. Sick Leave : Accrues at a rate of 12 days per academic year with unlimited accumulation. Pay Options : Faculty on academic year appointments have the option of receiving their salary paid in 10 payments (September 1 through June 1) or 12 payments (September 1 through August 1) each year. Optional Benefits Voluntary Life Insurance : Additional amounts of life insurance may be purchased on employee, spouse and dependent children. Voluntary Vision Plan : May enroll within the first 31 days of employment date. Job Summary/Basic Function Indiana State University’s Department of Engineering and Applied Sciences is seeking applications for a Tenure Track Assistant Professor or Multi-Year Contract Instructor. Duties include undergraduate courses in the Aviation degree programs. This is a nine-month position with the possibility of summer teaching assignments. Specific Responsibilities Reporting to the Chair of the Department, this position will teach, research, and provide service to the Department. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate courses in any of the following disciplines; Professional Aviation Flight Technology or Aviation Management. For the tenure-track position additional duties include serving on university committees, curriculum development, academic advisement and performing appropriate scholarly research and professional service within the guidelines of the University. Required Relevant Education & Experience Instructor rank: Master’s Degree Aviation, Education, Business or other related field. Tenure Track rank: PhD in Aviation, Education, Business or other related field with focus on aviation. ABD candidates will be considered but PhD must be completed by May 2027. Required Field(s) of Study Preferred Relevant Education and Experience Experience in the Aviation Industry. At least one aviation-focused degree for tenure track position Previous teaching experience and curriculum development Supervisory Responsi